Creational Pattern


1. Singleton Pattern 
Problem:

You want only one instance of a class throughout the application.

Examples:

Logger
Database connection pool
Configuration manager
Cache manager


Without Singleton
Logger logger1 = new Logger();
Logger logger2 = new Logger();

Two loggers created → wasteful.


class Logger {

    private static Logger instance;

    private Logger(){}

   public synchronized static Logger getInstance(){

    if(instance == null){
        instance = new Logger();
    }

    return instance;
}
}




2. Factory Pattern 

Problem:
Avoid creating objects directly.

Instead of:
EmailNotification email = new EmailNotification();
Client should not know implementation details.


Example:

Notification System:

          Notification
              |
    ---------------------
    |         |          |
 Email      SMS       Push



Factory:

class NotificationFactory {

public Notification getNotification(String type){

    if(type.equals("EMAIL"))
        return new EmailNotification();

    else if(type.equals("SMS"))
        return new SMSNotification();

    return new PushNotification();
}

}

Client:

Notification n = factory.getNotification("EMAIL");
n.send();



Benefits:

Object creation centralized
Easy adding new types
Loose coupling


Example:
Tomorrow:
WhatsappNotification
Just modify factory.



3. Abstract Factor is factory of Factories






4. Builder Pattern 

Very common in Java interviews.

Problem:
Constructor with many parameters.

Example:

class Notification {

    private String title;
    private String message;
    private String imageUrl;
    private String deepLink;
    private String priority;
    private boolean silent;

    private Notification(Builder builder) {
        this.title = builder.title;
        this.message = builder.message;
        this.imageUrl = builder.imageUrl;
        this.deepLink = builder.deepLink;
        this.priority = builder.priority;
        this.silent = builder.silent;
    }

    public static class Builder {

        private String title;
        private String message;
        private String imageUrl;
        private String deepLink;
        private String priority = "NORMAL";
        private boolean silent = false;

        public Builder title(String title) {
            this.title = title;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder message(String message) {
            this.message = message;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder imageUrl(String imageUrl) {
            this.imageUrl = imageUrl;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder deepLink(String deepLink) {
            this.deepLink = deepLink;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder priority(String priority) {
            this.priority = priority;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder silent(boolean silent) {
            this.silent = silent;
            return this;
        }

        public Notification build() {
            return new Notification(this);
        }
    }
}



